From ebb3ea558cdd87c01367d0a6d2121bf2127a97c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:45:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: map twiddled targets through GPU staging, clear
 depth on the GPU

- A CPU map of a twiddled/TFBC colour target goes through a linear
  staging resource: the GPU decodes the target into it (unless the map
  discards the whole content) and, after a write, encodes it back on
  unmap. The copy is one render whose background object reads the source
  (pvr_draw_blit, a load source for the existing load background). Maps
  of such targets used to fail, so glReadPixels on an FBO returned an
  error and CPU uploads into render-target textures were lost.
- Every full depth clear is the render's background depth (ZLS), opening a
  render that reloads colour if no colour clear opened one. The CPU path
  could not write a twiddled depth buffer, so a depth clear without a
  colour clear was dropped.
- The framebuffer target choice (with the depth-only scratch target) is a
  helper shared by draws and clears.
- Remove the test-only PVR_TWIDDLED_RAW_READBACK and PVR_FORCE_LINEAR_RT
  hooks and the per-draw getenv(PVR_NATIVE_COMPUTE_FALLBACK).
- pvr_probe: pass the new twiddled/fbc arguments to pvr_csb_pbe_words();
  the full build failed since the TFBC patch.

gltri: all modes match zink through the twiddled readback, and the new
GLTRI_SUBIMG (glTexSubImage2D into the rendered target) matches too.
---
